<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Starving Time</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1609">1609</a>–<a href="/years/1610">1610</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Starving Time was the winter of 1609–1610 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, when most of the English colonists died of famine and disease. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> cite it as evidence of the precariousness of early English colonisation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. Jamestown nonetheless survived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/starving-time.jpg" alt="Starving Time" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Beary (via Royall Bascom Smithey) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sickness_at_Jamestown_pp41_historyofvirgini00smith_0047_1898.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
